WEBVTT

00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:12.980
Did you finish your draft 
of the website update?

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:19.120
I'm almost finished. I'm not good with 
computers, so I had to do it analogue.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:24.320
"Their delightfully rising singing 
voices cause a sense of elation

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:29.130
as though I'm watching a musical."

00:00:30.370 --> 00:00:31.920
What a great comment.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.720
It's not that good.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:39.720
"Their musical sensibility is exceptional."

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:46.250
It looks like our president wasn't 
wrong to pull you out of that CD shop.

00:00:47.660 --> 00:00:50.230
I don't understand it myself.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:57.360
But if there's anything I can do 
for B-Pro, I'll work even harder.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:38.280
It's not going well.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:40.680
Yeah, we fumbled in the middle.

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:44.950
Tomo, the studio was narrower than that.

00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:48.770
Should we try moving to the front sooner?

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:51.280
Let's try it again from the top.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.320
All right!

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:52.320
Yeah.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.080
Yeah.

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:56.560
Guys, you've been dancing 
for three hours straight.

00:02:57.960 --> 00:03:00.400
Your attention, please.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:04.330
You can practice hard, 
but you have to take breaks, too.

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.870
What are you going to do 
if you hurt yourselves

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.910
when you have a recording 
for a TV show coming up?

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:11.150
You're right.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.580
Then let's take a break.

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:18.260
Good boys. Here, this is for you.

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:23.910
<b>"My 48-Hour
 Report"</b>

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.720
It's a report on the other day's RAIZIN Festival.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:28.020
<b>"The intensity of the performance even 
blew away the gathered storm clouds.
 Their staging exceeded expectations.
 Keep an eye on B-Project." (Nishiyama)</b>

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:28.020
Nishiyama-san commented on B-Project.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:32.270
"The intensity of the performance even 
blew away the gathered storm clouds."

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:36.020
"Their staging exceeded expectations."

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:39.780
"Keep an eye on B-Project."

00:03:40.040 --> 00:03:47.270
That's not all. Even <i>Kiss & Hug</i> asked 
to do a special article on B-Project.

00:03:47.270 --> 00:03:48.040
What?

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:52.540
The offer came directly from the editor. 
The shoot is tomorrow.

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:54.760
It's time.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:58.170
It's time to show them 
the fruits of your training, Gochin.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:00.670
Shut up.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:07.410
This is proof the world is starting 
to pay attention to B-Project.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.180
Yeah.

00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:11.140
Tomo, do you have a second?

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.780
I want to confirm the timing before the chorus.

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:16.270
Sure.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.650
<b>Monthly Sum of 2 Million Yen?!</b>

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.650
<b>With Someone 3 Years 
Younger Than His Daughter</b>

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:26.820
Momotasu, what are you reading?

00:04:27.350 --> 00:04:29.280
Hey, that's Matsukura-san's...

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:31.410
Lover scandal?

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:39.620
His performances are incredible. 
The air changes around him.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.340
Yeah. His fight scenes 
are the best in the industry.

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.760
<b>Monthly Sum of 2 Million Yen?!</b>

00:04:40.250 --> 00:04:43.760
<b>With Someone 3 Years 
Younger Than His Daughter</b>

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:45.740
Ryuji.

00:04:45.740 --> 00:04:48.390
Sorry. I'm going to go wash my face.

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.350
A lover, huh?

00:04:52.650 --> 00:04:55.600
You think Matsukura-san 
is popular with women?

00:04:56.310 --> 00:04:57.910
Well, he is a dandy.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.480
Yeah.

00:04:59.480 --> 00:05:05.160
I want to be dandier, too. 
Do you think I should grow out my beard?

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:07.810
You don't have a beard.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:10.740
What? It'll grow in soon.

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:13.620
Are dandies popular with the ladies?

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:17.670
Wouldn't that be Aizome-sensei's 
area of expertise?

00:05:18.580 --> 00:05:23.170
Before discussing popularity, we must 
first define what it means to be popular.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:25.380
What it means to be popular?

00:05:26.150 --> 00:05:28.460
Do you want to be loved deeply

00:05:28.460 --> 00:05:31.450
by a single person or broadly 
and shallowly by numerous women?

00:05:32.080 --> 00:05:33.710
Of course, both are sinful.

00:05:35.710 --> 00:05:37.310
He's so mature!

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.080
Huh?

00:05:38.440 --> 00:05:42.170
Hey, isn't Matsukura-san Kore-san's dad?

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:45.400
Now that you mention it, you're right.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:47.400
What? Really?

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:49.910
Ryu-chin, is it true?

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:52.480
Huh? He's not here.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:54.770
Maybe he's in the bathroom.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:59.530
Did all you guys know about this?

00:05:59.530 --> 00:06:01.310
No, it's news to me.

00:06:01.310 --> 00:06:03.900
Well, they hadn't made it public.

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:09.460
Isn't his mom an actress and 
his sister a top stylist?

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.220
So they're a super-elite family 
of the entertainment industry.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:14.030
Kane-chin, did you know?

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:16.350
No. I don't care, either.

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.200
Why doesn't Ryu-chin brag about it?

00:06:19.640 --> 00:06:21.800
Because people say all kinds of things.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:23.750
He probably doesn't want to cause any trouble.

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:28.950
And a family's circumstances 
can sometimes be complicated.

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:39.710
There he is. It's Korekuni Ryuji-kun.

00:06:40.120 --> 00:06:44.260
Could you tell me a little about your dad?

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:45.220
What?

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:51.720
<b>The Compensation is a Monthly Sum of 2 Million Yen?!</b>

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:51.720
This is really making waves. 
I want to make a splash with my next story.

00:06:53.000 --> 00:06:55.850
Do you know anything about 
the major actress you dad was

00:06:55.850 --> 00:07:00.170
rumored to be with or the beautiful woman 
he set up a business for in Kagurazaka?

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:02.760
No.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:08.870
There you go again. I heard you used 
to be bullied because of your dad while you

00:07:08.870 --> 00:07:11.970
were attending some training 
school called Bambi.

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:15.160
Kitakore.

00:07:15.850 --> 00:07:17.040
THRIVE.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:18.790
MooNs.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:25.540
The ten members of these three 
groups are the members of B-Project.

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:37.190
Must be nice to have an influential dad.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:40.540
You get to debut without doing anything at all.

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.940
My dad has nothing to do with it.

00:07:43.940 --> 00:07:47.400
Yeah, yeah. We can't hear you 
over your parents' influence.

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.700
Hey!

00:07:50.410 --> 00:07:53.610
Those aren't the faces of idols.

00:07:54.430 --> 00:07:56.620
They're black with envy.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:58.320
Shut up.

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:05.330
Don't let them keep you from smiling.

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:09.340
You have your own light, Ryuji.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:12.760
Tomo.

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:22.330
Does he have a secret love child?

00:08:23.580 --> 00:08:28.440
I don't know how many women he has, 
but you must know at least one of them, right?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.780
Ryu-chan.

00:08:36.160 --> 00:08:39.030
All I had to do was stir him up 
a little to make him turn pale.

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.610
Looks like I can expect to hear 
something about Matsukura from him.

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:47.840
I'll keep chasing, chasing, 
chasing Korekuni Ryuji.

00:08:54.640 --> 00:08:56.150
Ryu-chan, wait!

00:08:58.840 --> 00:08:59.940
Ryu-chan!

00:09:09.490 --> 00:09:10.400
Ryuji...

00:09:24.170 --> 00:09:25.200
Tomohisa.

00:09:25.790 --> 00:09:26.720
How's Ryuji?

00:09:28.680 --> 00:09:32.450
He's regained consciousness. He'll live.

00:09:33.810 --> 00:09:35.170
Good.

00:09:35.540 --> 00:09:40.310
But since he struck his head, they'll be 
keeping him at the hospital for a while.

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:44.800
Doctor, the patient in room 301...

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:54.300
The prince's dad runs this hospital.

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:56.380
I see...

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:58.170
They have the newest facilities and equipment,

00:09:58.170 --> 00:10:00.530
and their staff is supposed to be top notch.

00:10:01.480 --> 00:10:03.740
Osari-kun, how are you feeling?

00:10:03.740 --> 00:10:07.500
Huh? Oh, yeah. I'm fine.

00:10:07.760 --> 00:10:10.170
Hikaru-kun, you're not feeling well?

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:12.540
What? Oh...

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:15.370
During the commercial shoot the other day,

00:10:15.370 --> 00:10:17.840
he got ahead of himself and 
fell into the river, remember?

00:10:18.520 --> 00:10:20.180
He caught a cold after that.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.680
Yeah, that's right. I have a cold.

00:10:23.360 --> 00:10:25.430
I'm glad that's all it is.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:35.940
Ryuji...

00:10:41.920 --> 00:10:42.940
Who are you?

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.450
Who? Ryu-chin, there you go again.

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:52.210
Don't talk to me like you know me, mister.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.960
M-Mister?

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:59.760
Hitting his head made him lose 
his memories past the age of seven.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.610
Memory loss, huh?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:10.940
My father said it was temporary, 
but there's no clear way to restore his memory.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:12.980
What? Then...

00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:16.940
Right now we have to accept 
these circumstances.

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:18.900
N-No...

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:23.830
Kitakado-san, I'm tired
now. I want to sleep.

00:11:25.410 --> 00:11:26.360
You're right.

00:11:30.220 --> 00:11:33.080
You should rest for now.

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:36.260
You can have this.

00:11:38.130 --> 00:11:40.970
It's for being nice to me.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:51.660
Thank you.

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:59.360
I think we'll still be able
to do tomorrow's job.

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.360
Will he be okay?

00:12:03.000 --> 00:12:06.440
Something may happen 
on the job to restore his memory.

00:12:07.210 --> 00:12:11.120
And Ryuji has agreed to it. 
Would that be all right?

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:15.470
Fine. But don't push yourselves too hard.

00:12:15.470 --> 00:12:18.140
If anything happens, reach out 
to the agency for help right away.

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:20.450
We'll help, too.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.630
Yeah.

00:12:27.440 --> 00:12:28.650
Good work today.

00:12:30.840 --> 00:12:33.990
Um, Korekuni-san's family...

00:12:34.750 --> 00:12:38.530
We got in touch with them, 
but they can't come.

00:12:38.530 --> 00:12:41.400
What? You mean because of work?

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:48.030
He must be lonely.

00:12:53.340 --> 00:12:55.070
This is Kitakado.

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:56.730
<i>It's me.</i>

00:12:57.170 --> 00:13:01.550
<i>We talked about it at the office, 
and the higher-ups understand how you feel.</i>

00:13:02.270 --> 00:13:03.480
Thank you.

00:13:04.060 --> 00:13:06.030
<i>No, thank you.</i>

00:13:06.660 --> 00:13:10.990
<i>You may be on the rise, but if 
something big were to happen now,</i>

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:13.310
<i>there's no telling what effect 
it would have on B-Project.</i>

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.510
<i>For the sake of your futures as well,</i>

00:13:16.510 --> 00:13:19.310
<i>we have to keep Ryu-chan's
memory loss a secret.</i>

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:20.960
I understand.

00:13:29.460 --> 00:13:33.140
Korekuni Ryuji is suffering
from memory loss?

00:13:39.250 --> 00:13:40.080
Ryuji...

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:43.000
There's no time!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:44.940
Let's start shooting!

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:45.720
Yes, sir!

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.890
Boy, they're tense.

00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:52.660
Well, he's a tough
cameraman to work with.

00:13:54.320 --> 00:13:55.350
Ugh.

00:13:55.790 --> 00:13:58.580
Ryuji, let's get you changed 
into your outfit first.

00:13:58.580 --> 00:13:59.350
Okay.

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:02.050
Kitakado-san, we're ready to do your makeup.

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:07.390
Ryuji, it's the white suit.
Your name is on it.

00:14:07.390 --> 00:14:09.050
Go find your own outfit, okay?

00:14:09.050 --> 00:14:11.410
Korekuni-san, this way.

00:14:14.800 --> 00:14:15.910
Did you find it?

00:14:16.970 --> 00:14:18.220
Korekuni-san?

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.500
Ryuji, are you okay?

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.170
Yeah.

00:14:26.170 --> 00:14:27.170
Why?

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:33.310
Why is he dressed like that?

00:14:33.600 --> 00:14:35.430
Interesting. Come here.

00:14:36.330 --> 00:14:37.330
Okay.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.980
Wh-What's going on?

00:14:44.700 --> 00:14:46.870
You know what Ryuji looks like.

00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:50.840
When he was little, his mother 
used to dress him up as a girl.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:54.490
Sometimes he even did 
modeling work dressed like that.

00:14:55.340 --> 00:14:56.740
True...

00:14:57.520 --> 00:15:00.060
His smile is really cute.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:03.650
Well, yeah.

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:34.030
<i>It was like the run-of-the-mill 
doodles of the wind</i>

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:43.540
<i>Its color even seeps into memories</i>

00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:55.980
<i>I don't like having people 
look inside my heart</i>

00:15:55.980 --> 00:16:00.680
<i>Putting it to words make 
it seem like it would break</i>

00:16:01.570 --> 00:16:03.190
What are you doing?

00:16:03.190 --> 00:16:04.380
Sorry!

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:08.080
Every second counts in photography!

00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:10.950
How many chances do you 
think that cost me, huh?

00:16:10.950 --> 00:16:12.560
What happened?

00:16:12.560 --> 00:16:15.560
He wasn't holding the reflector properly.

00:16:15.560 --> 00:16:20.700
He's famous for getting out of hand 
once something makes him mad.

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.580
We'll probably have to take a break.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:25.670
You idiot!

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:26.170
Hey.

00:16:26.520 --> 00:16:27.170
What?

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.920
Why are you so mad?

00:16:30.280 --> 00:16:31.800
Stop, Ryu-chan.

00:16:31.800 --> 00:16:34.300
Here. Do you want some Chopa Chops?

00:16:34.300 --> 00:16:38.180
When you get mad at people, 
they make even more mistakes.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.170
What are you talking about?

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:43.440
So this is what you say.

00:16:45.020 --> 00:16:48.190
Mistakes, mistakes, fly away.

00:16:49.100 --> 00:16:51.940
Now you won't make any more.

00:16:54.990 --> 00:16:56.200
You...

00:17:00.750 --> 00:17:03.200
You're hilarious! You're really funny!

00:17:03.600 --> 00:17:06.040
All right!

00:17:06.040 --> 00:17:07.210
Ryuji.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:10.410
Sorry for wasting your time.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:11.740
Let's take some more pictures.

00:17:11.740 --> 00:17:12.960
Yes, sir!

00:17:13.640 --> 00:17:15.270
Nice, Ryuji.

00:17:15.930 --> 00:17:18.220
Ba-dump! That was amazingly cute.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:26.190
Kitakado-san...

00:17:32.340 --> 00:17:33.470
Korekuni-san?

00:17:34.480 --> 00:17:35.030
Ryuji?

00:17:35.030 --> 00:17:37.500
Kitakado, let's take some
pictures! Get in there!

00:17:37.500 --> 00:17:38.990
Sorry, Tsubasa. Go after him.

00:17:38.990 --> 00:17:40.130
I'll catch up later.

00:17:40.550 --> 00:17:41.470
Got it.

00:17:47.510 --> 00:17:49.750
Opportunity has arrived.

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.130
Korekuni-san!

00:17:59.320 --> 00:18:00.980
What's gotten into you?

00:18:01.960 --> 00:18:04.470
If we don't return to the
studio, the photo shoot...

00:18:04.470 --> 00:18:06.480
No. I'm not going back.

00:18:06.900 --> 00:18:07.500
What?

00:18:07.960 --> 00:18:10.980
I'm not doing the shoot. 
I'm not going to be an idol.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:12.500
I quit!

00:18:14.380 --> 00:18:19.080
I don't remember anything 
about Kitakore or B-Project.

00:18:20.610 --> 00:18:25.800
I only came because 
Kitakado-san said it would be okay.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:27.090
Korekuni-san...

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:32.870
But Kitakado-san won't look at me at all. 
He won't give me any attention.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.510
The two of you were laughing 
and having fun together.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:41.950
That's because we were talking about you.

00:18:41.950 --> 00:18:42.760
What?

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:49.060
He's not just cute or handsome.

00:18:49.940 --> 00:18:52.120
His strong will projects its own light.

00:18:52.970 --> 00:18:54.330
You can see it in Ryuji's smile.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:19:00.110
There's a light in my smile?

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:09.540
<i>Fragile like the stars and sad like the moon</i>

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:19.130
<i>I'll always illuminate 
only you from this place</i>

00:19:10.060 --> 00:19:12.330
Is this... me...?

00:19:13.230 --> 00:19:20.340
Like Kitakado-san said, 
your smile really does glow.

00:19:19.550 --> 00:19:28.200
<i>I want to protect that somehow 
sad and downcast smile</i>

00:19:22.630 --> 00:19:23.870
What's wrong?

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:28.650
I'm not sure, but I know now.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:35.090
<i>I just want to look at you</i>

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:29.360
What?

00:19:30.730 --> 00:19:33.590
That I love this job.

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:36.880
Have your memories returned?

00:19:35.570 --> 00:19:43.040
<i>Unable to even make casual remarks</i>

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:43.040
So you do have amnesia, Korekuni-kun.

00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:46.490
This'll make for a double scandal 
with Matsukura Kenzo's affair.

00:19:47.230 --> 00:19:49.290
Who is he? I'm scared.

00:19:49.290 --> 00:19:52.000
Go back to the studio, Korekuni-san.

00:19:52.470 --> 00:19:56.550
You lost your memories, but you still 
remember how to flirt with a girl, do you?

00:19:57.440 --> 00:19:59.710
You really are your father's son.

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:00.840
Please stop!

00:20:02.070 --> 00:20:02.760
You're not getting away!

00:20:08.160 --> 00:20:09.600
Yuta, I'm counting on you!

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:12.940
Korekuni-san!

00:20:13.200 --> 00:20:14.520
Hey, wait!

00:20:16.270 --> 00:20:16.930
Ryuji!

00:20:35.210 --> 00:20:36.060
Tomo...

00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.240
Ryuji.

00:20:42.770 --> 00:20:43.680
Yeah.

00:20:56.330 --> 00:20:57.190
Now then...

00:20:57.460 --> 00:21:00.130
That was really something
you did to our client.

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:03.010
What? I'll write an article about this.

00:21:03.010 --> 00:21:07.200
Matsukura Kenzo's son, 
Korekuni Ryuji, suffers from amnesia.

00:21:07.200 --> 00:21:08.330
There's nothing more interesting than—

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.760
Who has amnesia?

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:14.960
There are more interesting 
things to write about than me.

00:21:15.770 --> 00:21:18.960
<i>Looks like I can expect to hear 
something about Matsukura from him.</i>

00:21:17.970 --> 00:21:22.210
We wouldn't mind going to court.

00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:29.720
We erased all of the data and backups 
on your computer and camera.

00:21:30.350 --> 00:21:34.480
We retrieved all the photographic 
evidence from your bag and car, too.

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:36.840
Damn it.

00:23:11.710 --> 00:23:13.910
Look at this!

00:23:14.200 --> 00:23:16.520
It's Ryu-chin the maiden.

00:23:18.950 --> 00:23:22.000
Wait, Ryu-chin! Stop!

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.250
<b>Data Erased.</b>

00:23:24.250 --> 00:23:27.630
My angel's smile, come back to me!

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:29.180
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:23:32.970 --> 00:23:36.590
It's not like you've forgotten everything, right?

00:23:43.320 --> 00:23:47.290
Well, it seems like you were worried about me.

00:23:49.050 --> 00:23:50.280
I guess I should say...

00:23:52.820 --> 00:23:54.100
Thanks.

00:23:56.190 --> 00:23:59.150
Hey, come closer.
